  {
   "title": "Small corpus",
   "text": "1.2 million words, versus hundreds of millions for the main languages. Frequency values are unreliable, so there are no frequency bands, only the all-words generators. The reference lexicon has 57,763 words, so generators, neighbourhood measures and cluster filters are rougher than for the main languages."
  },
  {
   "title": "Wikipedia vocabulary added",
   "text": "49,729 of the reference words come from a Wikipedia corpus (Leipzig Corpora Collection, ckb_wikipedia_2021_100K, 1.7 million words); 8,034 come from the subtitle list. Written sources are more formal than subtitles and contain more names and foreign words. Frequencies of the corpus-only words come from that corpus and are not comparable with subtitle frequencies."
  },
  {
   "title": "Abjad: CV is orthographic",
   "text": "Sorani Kurdish writes most vowels. CV here is orthographic: ا ە ۆ ێ و ی count as V; و and ی are also consonants (w, y), which this rule cannot tell apart. Latin-script (Kurmanji) entries in the source were dropped."
  }
